comments[20]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-23T20:29:25.711Z","harness:codex","Implementation start 2026-08-23: selected after complete 2,538-item all-status inventory, live blocker verification, focused duplicate searches, and full metadata/comments/notes/relationship reads. This branch implements one coupled SDK/CLI/MCP composability tranche: newline/comma stdin and @path bulk-id selectors, close/update unmatched receipt parity, no/partial-effect exits, and an executable read-to-jq-to-write pipeline. Canonical lineage is reused; no duplicate item was created."
  "2026-08-23T22:05:18.038Z","harness:codex","Verification evidence 2026-08-24: bulk update/close IDs accept inline comma/newline text, readonly SDK arrays, stdin via '-', and @path files through one SDK-owned resolver with stable trim/dedupe. Explicit-ID close receipts now match update-many unmatched semantics, including empty unmatched arrays when all requested IDs exist, while existing-but-filtered IDs are not mislabeled missing. A disposable tracker proved list | jq | update-many --ids -, filter-only preview, body stdin, and cleanup. Final proof: 570 files / 7,858 tests pass; exact coverage is statements 57,420/57,420, branches 42,968/42,968, functions 11,955/11,955, lines 55,350/55,350; pnpm typecheck, secret scan, full lint/static assurance, contract snapshots, SDK surface, graph composition, record integrity, and PM governance all pass."
  "2026-08-23T22:06:25.447Z","harness:codex","Changelog evidence: installed pm-changelog 2026.8.17, regenerated package-owned CHANGELOG.md after closure, and the deterministic check passes."
  "2026-08-23T22:07:32.288Z","harness:codex","Self-review finding: history-compact also declares a bulk --ids selector. Extend the same SDK-owned scalar/array/newline/stdin/@path grammar to its CLI and MCP adapters and invocation contracts; do not ship the update/close-only gap."
  "2026-08-23T22:10:57.451Z","harness:codex","Self-review fix evidence: history-compact now resolves CLI --ids through the shared stdin/@path parser, MCP arrays use the same newline/comma stable-deduplicating grammar, action schemas accept string or array, and invocation contracts declare argv/file/stdin. Focused real-process and adapter tests pass 100/100."
  "2026-08-23T22:25:06.165Z","harness:codex","Final expanded-tree evidence 2026-08-24: real history-compact stdin transport is included. Exact full coverage passes 570 files / 7,858 tests at statements 57,419/57,419, branches 42,968/42,968, functions 11,953/11,953, and lines 55,349/55,349. Full pnpm lint passes ESLint, zero-clone detection, repository/static/contract/SDK gates, refusal closure, defect evidence, graph composition, and record integrity."
  "2026-08-23T22:39:08.160Z","harness:codex","Review findings: Bugbot P1 on --ids - combined with other stdin mutation fields, plus P2 because file input metadata omitted the required @ prefix. Security review independently confirmed the availability risk. Fix at the command-wide stdin consumer and typed invocation-contract boundaries with real-process negative controls."
  "2026-08-23T22:48:44.684Z","harness:codex","Review-fix evidence 2026-08-24: every create, update, update-many, and close-many invocation counts stdin-consuming tokens before any read. --ids - combined with --body -, --description -, --body-file -, structured fields, or --stdin-json now fails deterministically with usage exit 2. Bulk ID invocation contracts explicitly publish file_token_prefix=@ for update-many, close-many, and history-compact. Focused real-process/unit proof passes, and the final full run passes 570 files / 7,858 tests with exact coverage: statements 57,427/57,427, branches 42,973/42,973, functions 11,954/11,954, lines 55,356/55,356."
  "2026-08-23T22:59:18.745Z","harness:codex","Security re-review finding: the downstream bulk-ID resolver trims its sentinel, but the command preflight compared raw values, so --ids ' - ' could bypass single-consumer enforcement. Normalize scalar and repeated values before counting and retain a real-process negative control."
  "2026-08-23T23:08:02.970Z","harness:codex","Second review-fix evidence 2026-08-24: scalar and repeated stdin tokens are trimmed before the pre-read ownership count, exactly matching bulk-ID and shared stdin resolver semantics. --ids ' - ' plus --body - now exits 2 in a real process. All linked tests pass with local_source_ref trust and zero failure categories; full proof remains 570 files / 7,858 tests with exact coverage statements 57,427/57,427, branches 42,977/42,977, functions 11,954/11,954, lines 55,356/55,356."
  "2026-08-23T23:19:04.323Z","harness:codex","Bugbot final re-review finding: the typed ids override narrowed the historical string|number scalar to string|array, while normalizeBulkIdsValue assumed every scalar had split(). Restore finite numeric scalar compatibility in the public type and normalizer, and add compile/runtime regressions."
  "2026-08-23T23:26:20.494Z","harness:codex","Final compatibility evidence 2026-08-24: PmBulkMutationFilterOptions again accepts the historical finite numeric scalar ID alongside string and readonly string arrays; normalizeBulkIdsValue coerces finite numbers and returns undefined for non-finite values, avoiding raw TypeError. Type tests, direct runtime/updateMany dispatch regressions, isolated linked tests, and the full 570-file / 7,858-test suite pass. Exact coverage: statements 57,429/57,429, branches 42,981/42,981, functions 11,954/11,954, lines 55,358/55,358."
  "2026-08-23T23:34:55.994Z","harness:codex","Security review finding on exact head 130fd7835: normalizeBulkIdsValue mapped NaN and Infinity to undefined, which removes the ID allowlist. Preserve explicit invalid input as a blank selector so update-many and close-many reject it before loading or mutating matching rows."
  "2026-08-23T23:47:47.520Z","harness:codex","Bugbot exact-head findings: keep extension-contributed ids arrays transport-native by limiting bulk normalization to dedicated update/close/history adapters; replace the nonexistent scripting client.updateMany example with PmClient.run; widen annotation receipt replication triggers to the full receipt vocabulary; and make description whitespace sentinels resolve consistently with the preflight/shared resolver."
  "2026-08-23T23:59:32.665Z","harness:codex","Final review-fix evidence 2026-08-24: non-finite numeric selectors now remain explicitly blank and hit the bulk fail-closed guard rather than erasing the allowlist; extension-contributed actions retain array-valued ids; update/close/history normalize only in dedicated adapters; description whitespace sentinels match preflight/resolver semantics; the SDK example uses PmClient.run; and annotation receipt triggers cover mutation and omission vocabulary. Focused proof passes 36/36, linked tests pass with local_source_ref trust and zero failure categories, and the full 570-file / 7,858-test suite passes exact coverage: statements 57,429/57,429, branches 42,983/42,983, functions 11,954/11,954, lines 55,358/55,358. Full lint/static assurance and security scan pass."
  "2026-08-24T00:00:48.049Z","harness:codex","Changelog closeout: regenerated CHANGELOG.md from all release-tag windows with tracked .agents/pm links after final closure; deterministic check passes with 2,186 closed items and 393,233 bytes."
  "2026-08-24T00:21:15.297Z","harness:codex","Exact-head Bugbot recurrence fixed 2026-08-24: annotation receipt replication now triggers on the nested omitted-group name contract and the normalized.full transport mapping. Dedicated positive tests prove each line activates the set, while near-miss name assignment and unrelated normalized deletion lines remain inactive. Focused gate passes 18/18; full exact verification passes 570 files / 7,858 tests with 100% coverage (57,429 statements, 42,983 branches, 11,954 functions, 55,358 lines); typecheck, lint/static assurance, package/SDK/contracts/graph/record gates, and security scan all pass."
  "2026-08-24T01:16:00.584Z","harness:codex","Hosted-review fix evidence 2026-08-24: invalid explicit MCP history selectors no longer disappear into an undefined allowlist. NaN, positive/negative Infinity, mixed invalid arrays, empty arrays, and unsupported objects now fail with usage code bulk_ids_input_empty before target selection, including when allOver is present. Finite numeric scalars and mixed string/number arrays normalize through the shared stable-deduplicating parser; generated tool schemas, SDK surface, executable recovery, type tests, and scripting docs match. CodeRabbit's 15 canonical groups vs 16 catalog rows comment is a false positive because the ratchets intentionally count 15 identities plus one alias. Verification: linked tests 16/16 passed with trusted local-source provenance; full suite 570 files / 7,864 tests; exact coverage statements 57,445/57,445, branches 42,995/42,995, functions 11,955/11,955, lines 55,374/55,374; lint, typecheck, contracts, SDK surface, static assurance, package boundary/parity, security scan, graph composition, and record integrity pass."
  "2026-08-24T01:50:45.135Z","harness:codex","Review recurrence evidence: nested update-many/close-many compatibility inputs now route explicit ids through the dedicated bulk normalizer, preserving finite numeric selectors and converting NaN, Infinity, mixed-invalid arrays, and malformed values to the blank-selector refusal instead of erasing the allowlist. PmClient.historyCompactBulk now accepts the public BulkIdsValue contract, normalizes before tracker access, and refuses invalid explicit selectors. Focused direct-client/runtime/history tests passed; typecheck, lint/static/security gates passed; linked tests passed 18/18 with trusted local source refs and zero failure categories; exact coverage passed 570 files and 7870 tests at 100% statements (57454/57454), branches (43003/43003), functions (11957/11957), and lines (55383/55383)."
  "2026-08-24T02:31:54.759Z","harness:codex","Review-fix evidence: stdin JSON is now source-aware for create/update, so a decoded description value of '-' remains literal data and never starts a second read from an exhausted stdin stream. Nested and direct SDK bulk selectors fail closed on non-string and non-finite explicit IDs. Focused real-process/unit suites passed; linked tests passed 18/18 with zero trust refusals; full exact coverage passed 570 files / 7870 tests at 100% statements, branches, functions, and lines."
